    "content": "76c635c (origin/master, origin/HEAD) Add check for number of corner points in ptaConvertToBox() * also for Issue 743, in pixWriteStreamBmp() check for colormap before   referencing in DEBUG clause\ned50092 Improve extracting image compression formats from filenames and extensions. * split out extension table lookup (getFormatFromExtension()) from   getImpliedFileFormat() * add prog/scaleimages.c, for filtered scaling of images in a directory. * add JPG to extension table * fix incorrect use of lept_free() in pdfio2.c.  Use LEPT_FREE in the library. * in case there is a request to write a 24 bit pix in bmp format,   add converter from 24 to 32 bits in bmpio, as suggested by Ger Hobbelt   in PR #684 and #685\n0215271 Support read/write of 4 sample/pixel rgba images in bmp format * Vlad Astakhov submitted a fix to allow reading rgba (ignoring the alpha).   Windows screengrabs apparently produce these. * Save the alpha component when reading rgba in bmp format. * For spp == 4 pix, save the alpha component when writing bmp. * Added a test section in ioformats_reg for miscellaneous tests.   In there, test write/read of rgba, including alpha, for both png and bmp.\n427de3e Remove PROCNAME / procName and use __func__\ne8b670d Split pix.h and array.h into a public interface and an internal interface * The internal files pix_internal.h and array_internal.h contain   definitions of the structs. * The rest is the public interface, with typedefs and flags. * Applications should use the public interface, which includes accessors   to the fields, but if necessary they can include the internal files. * Only twelve test programs in /prog require an internal file to be included. * These changes were suggested and promoted by Stefan Weil.  They are   a significant change to the ABI and will require increasing the .so   number of the library to 6.0.0.\nd4ab740 Make bmpio non-support of 32-bit bmp (rgba) explicit * leptonica support for bmp files is intended to be minimal: 1,2,4,8,16   bpp with 1 component; 24 bpp for RGB; 4 byte colormaps up to 256 colors;   no compression; no transparency. * 32 bpp bmp files made by windows screen grab have transparency and are   not supported.  Use png for images with transparency. * Decision not to support 32-bit bmp files may be revised in the future.\n7c42450 Fix oss-fuz issues 22377 and 22378: leaks during writing png * Make sure that colormap is valid * Also check validity for writing bmp, gif, spix\ne1d5c88 Fixed oss-fuzz issue 22323: Direct-leak in pixcmapCreate() * Always attach colormap to pix, even if not valid. * Check pixSetColormap() in I/O routines where the pix and colormap   depths may differ.\n6988379 Better handling of 1 bpp colormapped images.  Also: * removal of duplicated code in rotate1_reg.c * adding clear notification in reg test output when errors are expected * add some error checking (dewarp1.c, utils2.c)\n002843b (tag: 1.79.0) Yet another small restriction on bmp input data.\n7a74abc More sanity-checking restrictions on input data in bmp files\n50c3c35 Fix bit shift overflow in bmp reading.\nbb6252d Improved sanity checking on colormap size when reading bmp files.\n9540500 (HEAD -> master) Modified bmpio allow reading from files with newer formats. * No longer restrict the infoheader to be 40 bytes. * Add 2 bpp bmp file to mtiff_reg test. * Addresses issue #454\n4f25104 Replaced all fprintf(stderr, ...) with lept_stderr(...) in the library * This completes the stderr redirection. * Also included auto_config.h in this set of about 80 changed files\n1480744 In gplot, generate the pix directly with a single call * without having to specify a rootname and then generating the   file name to read it back.  This is done changing only       gplotSimpleXY1(), ...XY2() and ... XYN()   and adding new functions that call them:       gplotSimplePix1(), gplotSimplePix2(), gplotSimplePixN() * Also, several small mods to satisfy various compilers * Also, begin adding #include <config_auto.h> to all source files.   This must be added at the top, as the first non-comment statement.   Richard Daniel also pointed out that you shouls use <> instead   of quotes to be sure to get the config file of the build system,   if there is one. * Also fixed some potential leaks found by Coverity Scan. CS has   been broken for about 6 months, but Stefan Weil was able to   load the previous version and run it.\na194247 Accommodate buggy readers that use the alpha byte with 3 bpp RGB images. * Some java tests have been trying to interpret the alpha byte for   RGB images.  We set the alpha byte to 255 (opaque), although it is   not necessary (issue #442). * Also, add caution about using orientation detector on tables (issue #466).\n18abe3c Removed 'register' from the auto-generated files * 'register' declarations were deprecated as of C++-11. * modified the auto-generation software and templates to   generate proper Doxygen comments * This involved fixing 3 of the code generators (fhmtauto.c,   fmorphauto.c, stringcode.c), 5 of the templates (hmttemplate*.txt,   morphtempalte*.txt, stringtemplate1.txt), and regenerating 9 source   files of auto-genned code (dwacomb*.c, dwalinear*.c, fhmtgen*.c,   fmorphgen*.c, autogen.137.c).  Not something you want to do very often. Also: * More use of uint32 to avoid fuzzer complaints about 32 bit left shifts.   Most likely this wasn't a problem. * Removal of some unused #defines. * Increment version numbers beyond current release, to 1.79.\na2d832e Strict constraint on size of headers, colormap and data in bmp file.\nca56c4e bmp: fix handling of bitmap file header\n5d4aca0 Fix signed int overflow in bmp reading * found by Google fuzzers * issue #378\n8398f6d Put the bmp packed header typedef in bmp.h, where it belongs. * As a result, the prototype parser, which only uses .c files and   has learned to ignore typedefs, never sees it anyway.\n698b12b Introduce `l_ok' return type for OK / error results.\n2818110 Fix bmpio for sparc64\n2e25464 Bmpio fixed to accept negative image height * For bmp, h < 0 means that the image is flipped top-to-bottom\nb88c821 New implementation of pixWordMaskByDilation() * more robust, simpler, faster, fewer input args, better debugging output * also simplified pixGetWordsInTextlines(), pixGetWordBoxesInTextlines(),   and jbWordsInTextlines(). * better reg test prog/wordboxes_reg. * also use jpeg output for large images in texturefill_reg.c, instead of   png. The test is now 6x faster and the output images are 7x smaller. * Changes in several other progs due to simpler interfaces above. * Bug fix for bmp reading to set opacity. * Fix for potential injection attack using gplot rootdir.\naf126bd More small improvements based on static code analysis: * logic simplifications * elimination of possible memory leaks * explicit casts from int to float where needed Also remove trailing spaces\n45f5dbb Simplification and speedup of separable unsharp masking operations. *  Also remove unused variables.\n309f1a8 New boxa geometric functions useful for mask processing: * boxaContainedInBoxa(), boxaCombineOverlapsInPair(), boxCompareSize() * coverity scan fixes for initializing; avoiding zero divide * also added reg test function for determining local filename.\n5f0d17f Fixed bmpio for both 16 bpp and 2 bpp * for 16 bpp, properly reads and writes, without a colormap * for 2 bpp, converts to 8 bpp, saving the colormap if it exists. * added two colormap depth converters * added 4th mode for converting 16 bpp --> 8 bpp\nb8cdbd9 bmp I/O is rewritten to implement the memory version directly. * This is relatively simple because we don't handle compression,   so the size of the memory buffer is easily calculated. * The stream read interface is then implemented, as with webp,   as a combination of a file read and memory deserialization. * Likewise, the stream write interface is implemented as a   combination of serialization to memory followed by writing to file. * This avoids writing temp files on all platforms.\nf42326c Improve baseline finder; fix dewarp bug * Promote baselinetest.c --> baseline_reg.c  (regression test) * Make debug output callable (without recompiling) * Fix bug in dewarp line finder where end points can get out of sync * Fix several coverity scan possible leaks. * Added another arabic scan for testing textline finding (in misctest1.c)\n8a839a2 Split utils.c into 2 files * utils1.c: various utilities * utils2.c: multi-platform and everything with strings * downgraded msg of work-around image I/O to memory, from WARNING to INFO\n4bb6ca6   Transition all *.c files to doxygen comment style.\n819c654 Doxygen: add a quick hack converter + Doxyfile\na9cd49b Remove unneeded extern declarations\nca9d16a Change fmemopen behavior, windows temp files.\nea93a43 Add leptonica 1.73.\n2d199fd (tag: v1.72) Add leptonica 1.72.\n8c68d3f (tag: v1.71) Add leptonica 1.71.\n10ea745 (tag: v1.70) Add leptonica 1.70.\n3cdf473 (tag: v1.69) Add leptonica 1.69.\n316b85b (tag: v1.67) Add leptonica 1.67.\na9adf23 (tag: v1.66) Add leptonica 1.66.\n68987bf (tag: v1.58) Add leptonica 1.58.\n129b067 (tag: v1.56) Add leptonica 1.56.\nc76a768 (tag: v1.54) Add leptonica 1.54.\n465dde1 (tag: v1.46) Add leptonica 1.46.\n8995727 (tag: v1.44) Add leptonica 1.44.\n51aa669 (tag: v1.42) Add leptonica 1.42.",
